# {{ project_name }}

The **Serial Hello** example sends `Hello from STM32 #N` about once per second over `{{ uart_peripheral }}`
and echoes received bytes. The LED on `{{ led_pin }}` blinks about once every two seconds.

## Target board

**{{ board_name_en }}** uses the `{{ chip_id }}` microcontroller with
{{ flash_kb }} KB of flash and {{ ram_kb }} KB of RAM. The Rust target is `{{ target_triple }}`.

## Connect a USB-to-UART adapter

| Board | Adapter |
| --- | --- |
| `{{ uart_tx_pin }}` (TX) | RX |
| `{{ uart_rx_pin }}` (RX) | TX |
| GND | GND |

Open the **UART** tab in NightExpress or use a serial terminal at **115200 baud, 8N1**.

## Build from the command line

```sh
cargo build --release
```

The firmware ELF is written to `target/{{ target_triple }}/release/{{ project_name }}`.
